// Design exploration index.
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>tvml-react docs: design exploration</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>tvml-react docs: design exploration</h1>
      <p>The same reference page (<code>Stack</code>) in three directions.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <a href="/explore/a">A. Faithful</a>
          <span>Apple's developer documentation as closely as possible: light, sidebar of symbols with kind badges, declaration box, Overview / Topics / See Also. The example is a code listing and a screenshot.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/explore/b">B. Apple, plus a live example panel</a>
          <span>Same chrome, but every example is a panel: the React source, the TVML it renders (produced at build time by running the example through tvml-react), and a capture from the tvOS simulator in a TV frame. Parameters as rows with type pills, See Also as cards.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/explore/c">C. tvOS-flavoured, runs in the browser</a>
          <span>Dark, glassy, focus-lift hover like tvOS. The example runs in the page: change align, gap and width and the scaled 1920×1080 preview and the code update together, with a toggle to the real simulator capture.</span>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  main {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 60px auto;
    font-family: -apple-system, sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  li {
    margin: 18px 0;
  }
  li a {
    display: block;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 19px;
  }
  li span {
    color: #555;
  }
</style>
